we're going to start today in australia  where progressives scored a massive  victory in the australian elections  those were on saturday dozens of you  emailing me about this and saying david  you've got to cover what's happening in  australia because not only is it a  massive victory for the left it's also a  big signal about what could be possible  maybe  in the united states if the united  states became significantly less crazy  and we'll get to that in a moment  the liberal party in australia led by  the prime minister scott morrison wanted  a fourth term in a row  and the opposition the main opposition  the strongest opposition was the  left-wing labour party led by anthony  albanese  votes are still being counted but it  does appear as of this morning as though  the labor party will have the ability to  form a government due to some major wins  that they had and as of right now and  again they're still counting votes these  numbers may change as of this morning i  should say  this morning australia time  labor looks to be up to 73 seats  while the liberal party appears to have  lost 24 seats from 75 before the  election  down to only 51. this is a big  defeat for the centrist liberal party  and it is a crushing victory  for the left wing labour party now also  of note the green party led by adam bant  appears to have secured three seats they  previously had one so gaining two from  one to three seats as of this morning  the green party although the final  numbers may change a little bit so this  would make anthony albanese the fourth  labor leader  and by the way i hope i'm pronouncing  that correctly the fourth labor leader  to win control of the government since  world war ii  so the first question is how on earth  did labor achieve this what did they run  on well a huge component of labor's 2022  platform  was climate change  it was a platform of  renewal not revolution  and labor making a number of promises  along the lines of the environment and  dealing with climate change labor  promised to nearly double australia's  2030 target cuts to carbon emissions  saying let's cut by 43 percent by 2030  and be it completely net zero by 2050  very ambitious is it possible to do that  well time will tell but they ran on it  and the voters liked it  transitioning to renewable energy  upgrade the nation's energy grid  roll out solar banks and community  batteries as many as many of you know  it's great that solar panels are  becoming more and more efficient but  you've got to be able to store that  energy to really increase the viability  of solar  at a larger level um the labour party  said that they would approve new coal  mines  if they stack up environmentally and  economically so not saying we're not  doing any more fossil fuels but saying  it's it's really got to make sense in  context a promise to keep the uh  australian great barrier reef more  protected to protect endangered species  to do more about bush fire recovery and  also campaigned on increasing  australia's federal national minimum  wage more funding for child care centers  nursing homes and disability services  and understand that this is not  communism  this is not socialism there were right  wingers all over twitter and all over  truth central and all of these other  places saying australia has gone  completely communist now the really  funny thing is  the various many of the very same people  would say that the liberal party was  also communist now understand the the  this is true  what i would call left center left  you've got the center  you've got the center left which would  be like the liberal party like justin  trudeau in canada more or less that's  center left and then you've got this is  not far left this is what i would call  left center left it's social democracy  it's certainly to the left of biden and  justin trudeau but it is not socialism  and it is not communism it's basically  where i am it's social democracy in  something more or less approximating the  nordic model the northern european model  so  understand that many of the same people  that are now saying oh australia has  elected socialists  they say justin trudeau is a socialist  they said that the australian liberal  party liberal party was also socialist  when they were not so these people you  can't really go to them this is going to  be a major experiment can labor  in power get things done  and maybe even more importantly are the  things labor wants to do  actually viable will they work because  another big  criticism of many of the ideas that i  and other social democrats espouse is  that stuff would never work if you had  the opportunity to make it law to make  it policy to actually do this stuff it  will implode your country it will be a  disaster for your country well let's see  and depending on the level of  obstruction that's possible in australia  we may in a few years have some answers  do these ideas actually work  despite what the right loves to say when  people like me and others propose them  in the united states so it's going to be  a fascinating time and this is  we can't shortchange what this is this  is a massive victory  for the left  running on climate change  environmental justice economic justice  renewable energy all of these things  we've been talking about a couple of  notes stephanie from australia wrote in  to me and said quote  one of the most interesting aspects of  this has been a large number of very  wealthy traditionally liberal party  inner city districts being taken by a  group of loosely aligned independents  who are economically moderate right but  pro action on climate change political  integrity and gender equality this is  being seen as a repudiation of the  conservative government's move to the  right towards a more republican style  would an independent movement like that  with funding from rich moderate  conservative backers as the case here  have any chance in similar areas of the  u.s well the question in the u.s is  i don't know that we have that group  i mean  i guess anecdotally there are some  center-right moderates who are quite  socially liberal and pro-action on  climate change  but i don't really know that that's  really a big contingent i mean here you  know if you if you think of the center  right in the united states and i know  everybody this is fraught because people  would say those aren't really  center-right people if you think of the  center right in the united states which  is people like joe manchin and mitt  romney  they don't seem big  on taking bold action on climate  uh they seem to really want to kind of  just protect business interests when it  comes to thinking about climate so sure  stephanie it would work if we had that  contingent in the united states i don't  know that we do but i'm willing to have  my mind changed also our friend josh  zepps  who i've been on his show i don't  remember if he's been on my show he's  australian he had a good tweet quote the  lesson of the australian election is  unambiguous if you refuse to address a  big problem that voters persistently say  they care about they'll smack you down  australians are fed up with excuses  about climate chaos they've been saying  this for years welcome to democracy  hopeful results  in australia a really big deal  as many of you know i'm a busy person i  don't always have the exact correct  nutritional plan for my meals every  single day and that's why i also take a  multivitamin and a couple of supplements  but doing them all separately can be a  little bit time-consuming which is why  athletic greens is just fantastic and  they're one of our sponsors i've been  using the athletic greens since last  year it just really simplifies nutrition  i just do a scoop of the ag-1 and i'm  getting 75 high-quality vitamins and  minerals and my probiotics and it's all  from whole food sources i drink it in  the morning i know i'm good i don't have  to be messing around with different  pills and supplements or whatever or  spend time planning when what time of  day do i need to take each one i just  get it all with one scoop you can put it  in a smoothie you can drink it straight  it tastes great and then i'm just good  for the day  it supports gut health and i'm getting  everything that i need and i'm looking  for athletic greens is giving my  audience a free one-year supply of  vitamin d plus five free travel packs  when you go to athleticgreens.com  pacman and the link is down below

